[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   aborts the rest of the format string. The four cases — 0, 1, 2 and 3
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   successful conversions — map to results 1, 2, 3 and 0 respectively, since `x`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   and `z` start at 0 and `y` at 123.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **`%d` skips whitespace across lines.** `\n`, `\t`, `\r`, `\v`, `\f` and runs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   of 100 000 spaces are all consumed transparently; `1\n2\n3` behaves the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   as `1 2 3`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Sign handling and matching failures.** `+1` converts; a lone `-`, `- 1`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `--1`, `++1`, `+-1`, `.1`, `abc` and `e` are all matching failures that assign
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   nothing.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Base 10 only.** `0x10` converts as `0` and leaves `x` at the `x`, which then
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   fails the next conversion. `010` is ten, not eight.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **Truncation to `int` is observable and reproduced.** `4294967297` truncates
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   to `1` and *passes* stage 1; `4294967298` for `y` passes stage 2;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `4294967299` for `z` passes stage 3. An input of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `4294967297 4294967298 4294967299` prints `Ok!` in both programs.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **glibc saturates before truncating.** The accumulator follows `strtol`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   semantics: values beyond `long` clamp to `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN` and only then
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   truncate to `int`, so `LONG_MAX as i32 == -1`. This is distinguishable from a
