[1mThe mismatch:[22m with stdout on a pipe whose reader had hung up, the C program was killed by [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m (signal 13, no exit code) while the Rust program exited 0. Cause: Rust's runtime installs [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m for [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m, so the failing write returned [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m, which the translation discards (correctly mirroring C ignoring [38;5;10mprintf[0m's return). Fixed by resetting the disposition to [38;5;10mSIG_DFL[0m at the top of [38;5;10mmain[0m. This was invisible to output comparison — both produced zero bytes — so only the exit-status assertion caught it.[0m[0m
