Two things worth noting about what turned out to be already correct. The translation's [38;5;10m%d[0m handling reproduces glibc's saturate-then-truncate semantics, which is observably different from a wrapping accumulator: [38;5;10m4294967297[0m truncates to [38;5;10m1[0m and passes the [38;5;10mx != 1[0m check, while [38;5;10m18446744073709551618[0m clamps to [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m and becomes [38;5;10m-1[0m rather than wrapping to [38;5;10m2[0m. And the pre-set global [38;5;10my = 123[0m is genuinely observable, since [38;5;10mscanf[0m writes into it and leaves it alone when the second conversion fails.[0m[0m
